\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Recording ordered fermion insertions}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The paired Gaussian formula in \ref{fdip-008H} gives the determinant as the coefficient integral of #{e^{-\bar\psi(K\psi)}}. Inserting other ordered products into the same integrand gives correlations. How can one finite polynomial record these insertions and their behavior under elimination?}
